Z||000000||Cheever3000||10-30-2001||01:50 PM||||YES!  An old dog CAN learn new tricks.  Thanks to the advice here, and to a new friend on the Fiero-List, I was able to change my alternator.  When I got the old one out, I saw there were several ball-bearings missing.  No wonder it was screaming like a banshee.  Help me give some love - well, gratitude at least - to ShinyGreenEyes@aol.com for selling me a used alternator for a very low price.  His name is Benjamin.  And thanks to my Forum pards for pushing me along.  I would have given up except for knowing you guys would be very disappointed in me if I couldn't do this myself.  Let's see, I've repaced a heater core, Duke exhaust manifold, headliner, A/C tube thing, radio, body parts, and now alternator.  Gimme five!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
